    "result_text": "Full suite green \u2014 277 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the per-city owner cap: **creating an owner is rejected with 400 once its city already contains 8 owners.**\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern used by the sibling rules (duplicate \u2192 409, daily limit \u2192 400), I added:\n\n1. **`EnforceOwnerCityLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose city matches the new owner's city (case-insensitively, consistent with `NormalizeOwnerCity`) and throws `OwnerCityLimitException` when the count is \u2265 8. Blank cities are exempt.\n2. **`OwnerCityLimitException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) and **`OwnerCityLimitExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the daily-limit handler.\n3. **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n4. **Wired** `enforceCityLimit` into `owners.POST.yml` between `enforceDailyLimit` and `normalizeCity`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\nOne existing test required adjustment: the cp13 daily-limit test (`createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached`) created all 20 same-day owners in \"Madison\" \u2014 incidental data that inherently conflicts with an 8-per-city cap. Its purpose is the per-*day* count, so I spread those owners across distinct cities (`DailyLimitCity00`\u2026`19`, and a fresh city for the rejected 21st), keeping them same-day. The daily limit still triggers the 400, and the city cap is no longer collaterally hit.\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests.coreRejectsOverCityCap` passes (8 accepted in a fresh city, 9th \u2192 400), and the full suite remains green.",
